WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:29.750


2
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.208
<b>In previous verses,</b>

3
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:32.375
<b>Lord Krishna explained</b>

4
00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:37.666
<b>how humans please the devas (divine beings) </b>
<b>through sacrificial offerings,</b>

5
00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:44.208
<b>and in return, the devas fulfill human </b>
<b>needs and desires.</b>

6
00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:45.708
<b>These sacrifices by humans</b>

7
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:51.500
<b>are a medium to express their gratitude </b>
<b>and appreciation towards the devas. </b>

8
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.583
<b>But</b>

9
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:59.458
<b>what of those who enjoy all the</b>
<b>facilities provided by the devas,</b>

10
00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:07.541
<b>yet show neither gratitude nor express </b>
<b>appreciation through sacrifices?</b>

11
00:01:07.541 --> 00:01:10.791
<b>This verse describes such people.</b>

12
00:01:11.458 --> 00:01:15.708


13
00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.791
<b>Lord Krishna states that</b>

14
00:01:18.791 --> 00:01:21.666
<b>while the devas, pleased with sacrifices,</b>

15
00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:25.583
<b>will certainly provide everything </b>
<b>according to human desires,</b>

16
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:32.250
<b>a person who enjoys life's gifts and facilities</b>

17
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:39.500
<b>without offering anything in return </b>
<b>is essentially a thief.</b>

18
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.500
<b>Think of it this way –</b>

19
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.458
<b>electricity</b>

20
00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:45.500
<b>is vital for modern human life,</b>

21
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.750
<b>but someone who uses electricity </b>
<b>abundantly in their home</b>

22
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:54.291
<b>yet never pays their bills or its cost</b>

23
00:01:54.291 --> 00:01:57.166
<b>would be called an electricity thief.</b>

24
00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:58.250
<b>Similarly,</b>

25
00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.041
<b>water,</b>

26
00:01:59.041 --> 00:01:59.750
<b>fire,</b>

27
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:00.541
<b>air,</b>

28
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:01.375
<b>education,</b>

29
00:02:01.375 --> 00:02:06.416
<b>energy – these are all fundamental necessities</b>

30
00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:09.708
<b>without which humans cannot survive.</b>

31
00:02:09.708 --> 00:02:15.541
<b>The responsibility for administering all these </b>
<b>departments of the universe lies with the devas.</b>

32
00:02:15.541 --> 00:02:22.041
<b>They are the ones who distribute these </b>
<b>resources throughout the universe efficiently.</b>

33
00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.166
<b>This raises a natural question –</b>

34
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:30.208
<b>what does humanity offer to the </b>
<b>devas in return for these facilities?</b>

35
00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:32.125
<b>What do they pay back?</b>

36
00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:33.416
<b>The truth is,</b>

37
00:02:33.416 --> 00:02:36.416
<b>humans own nothing themselves.</b>

38
00:02:36.416 --> 00:02:40.750
<b>Whatever they receive existed before their birth</b>

39
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.916
<b>and will remain after their death.</b>

40
00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:45.666
<b>Humans must understand</b>

41
00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:51.458
<b>that they have no true ownership over </b>
<b>any resource or facility on Earth.</b>

42
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:53.750
<b>This is why it becomes their responsibility</b>

43
00:02:53.750 --> 00:03:02.000
<b>to protect these facilities gifted by the </b>
<b>devas and use them in moderation.</b>

44
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.750
<b>This understanding will make </b>
<b>humans humble and grateful.</b>

45
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.750
<b>Moreover,</b>

46
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:15.583
<b>humans can only express their gratitude by considering </b>
<b>all things in life as infinite grace from the devas.</b>

47
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:20.083
<b>Sacrifice is a medium to express this gratitude.</b>

48
00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:23.916
<b>Just as someone takes a dip in Mother Ganges</b>

49
00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:28.458
<b>and offers that same water back</b>
<b>to her in their palms,</b>

50
00:03:28.458 --> 00:03:35.875
<b>humans too can only offer back to the </b>
<b>devas what they received from them.</b>

51
00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:40.500
<b>The devas are not dependent on our response.</b>

52
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:46.541
<b>However, maintaining a constant feeling of </b>
<b>gratitude towards them is essential for humans.</b>

53
00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:49.041
<b>This represents their culture,</b>

54
00:03:49.041 --> 00:03:52.875
<b>and this mutual relationship </b>
<b>between devas and humans</b>

55
00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:56.666
<b>keeps creation running smoothly.</b>

56
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:03.833
<b>Think for a moment...</b>

57
00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:05.708
<b>How would you feel</b>

58
00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:13.875
<b>if someone constantly took things </b>
<b>from you and enjoyed them,</b>

59
00:04:13.875 --> 00:04:18.083
<b>yet never showed any gratitude?</b>

60
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:22.166
<b>While you may not need a formal thank you,</b>

61
00:04:22.166 --> 00:04:29.500
<b>surely you'd agree that we're naturally</b>
<b>inclined to help those who show appreciation.</b>

62
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.666
<b>Now imagine</b>

63
00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:35.125
<b>after using your belongings for so long,</b>

64
00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:47.083
<b>if this person began claiming </b>
<b>complete ownership of them.</b>

65
00:04:47.083 --> 00:04:49.875
<b>Isn't this deceitful?</b>

66
00:04:49.875 --> 00:04:53.166
<b>Wouldn't such a person be considered a thief?</b>

67
00:04:53.166 --> 00:04:58.416
<b>Reflect again.</b>

68
00:04:58.416 --> 00:05:03.333
<b>Humans live their lives in much the same way.</b>

69
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:11.291
<b>They not only use life's comforts </b>
<b>and resources ungratefully</b>

70
00:05:11.291 --> 00:05:12.166
<b>but</b>

71
00:05:12.166 --> 00:05:18.250
<b>begin to claim ownership over them.</b>

72
00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:27.000
<b>As if the earth and universe exist</b>
<b>solely to provide for them.</b>

73
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.791
<b>What a profound mistake,</b>

74
00:05:29.791 --> 00:05:32.625
<b>what a misguided belief.</b>

75
00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:39.166
<b>Humans must develop an attitude of</b>
<b>gratitude rather than ownership.</b>

76
00:05:39.166 --> 00:05:41.666
<b>This becomes possible</b>

77
00:05:41.666 --> 00:05:43.750
<b>only when you acknowledge</b>

78
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.000
<b>that your capabilities,</b>

79
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.208
<b>resources,</b>

80
00:05:47.208 --> 00:05:48.208
<b>education,</b>

81
00:05:48.208 --> 00:05:51.333
<b>wealth, and everything else you've accumulated</b>

82
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:54.541
<b>isn't solely your doing.</b>

83
00:05:54.541 --> 00:06:01.958
<b>Many people and factors made this possible –</b>

84
00:06:01.958 --> 00:06:03.541
<b>your parents,</b>

85
00:06:03.541 --> 00:06:05.041
<b>your teachers,</b>

86
00:06:05.041 --> 00:06:07.875
<b>your supporters, and countless others.</b>

87
00:06:07.875 --> 00:06:13.125
<b>A person of character never forgets others' help,</b>

88
00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:16.333
<b>remaining humble and grateful always.</b>

89
00:06:16.333 --> 00:06:18.958
<b>This is the key to a fulfilled life.</b>

90
00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:24.416
<b>I hope, you wouldn't want to </b>
<b>be known as deceitful or a thief.</b>

91
00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:31.500
<b>Be genuinely grateful for every person and </b>
<b>circumstance that aids your journey.</b>

92
00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.708
<b>And yes,</b>

93
00:06:32.708 --> 00:06:34.666
<b>- the breath you take,</b>

94
00:06:34.666 --> 00:06:37.416
<b>the water you drink, the food you eat,</b>

95
00:06:37.416 --> 00:06:39.750
<b>and the fire that cooks it</b>

96
00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.791
<b>and for such countless priceless gifts</b>

97
00:06:42.791 --> 00:06:49.416
<b>it's essential to remember and </b>
<b>honor the Divine, the deities.</b>

98
00:06:49.416 --> 00:06:51.291
<b>"For this life</b>

99
00:06:51.291 --> 00:06:58.666
<b>and everything in it, I am simply </b>
<b>and completely grateful."</b>

100
00:06:58.666 --> 00:07:02.333
<b>You just need to remember this mantra.</b>

101
00:07:07.083 --> 00:07:10.416
<b>Family is a beautiful system</b>

102
00:07:10.416 --> 00:07:15.958
<b>that not only helps preserve our culture</b>

103
00:07:15.958 --> 00:07:17.166
<b>but</b>

104
00:07:17.166 --> 00:07:19.583
<b>nurtures mutual love</b>

105
00:07:19.583 --> 00:07:20.458
<b>and</b>

106
00:07:20.458 --> 00:07:26.500
<b>enables us to progress in </b>
<b>life through mutual support.</b>

107
00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:32.000
<b>This family system works most beautifully</b>

108
00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.166
<b>when there's a balance between </b>
<b>duty and gratitude.</b>

109
00:07:36.166 --> 00:07:45.666
<b>While the elders take responsibility for nurturing,</b>
<b>protecting, and guiding the young,</b>

110
00:07:45.666 --> 00:07:54.541
<b>the younger members respond with </b>
<b>their obedience and respectful gratitude.</b>

111
00:07:54.541 --> 00:07:55.458
<b>But</b>

112
00:07:55.458 --> 00:08:00.833
<b>is gratitude merely saying thank you?</b>

113
00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:02.541
<b>Indeed,</b>

114
00:08:02.541 --> 00:08:06.875
<b>expressing verbal appreciation is a good start,</b>

115
00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:11.541
<b>but true gratitude runs much deeper.</b>

116
00:08:11.541 --> 00:08:15.458
<b>Gratitude becomes genuine</b>

117
00:08:15.458 --> 00:08:26.458
<b>only when you deeply understand how </b>
<b>selflessly others strive to fulfill your needs.</b>

118
00:08:26.458 --> 00:08:28.708
<b>Look at a mother,</b>

119
00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.708
<b>who patiently</b>

120
00:08:30.708 --> 00:08:36.625
<b>cares for her children and other family members.</b>

121
00:08:36.625 --> 00:08:39.625
<b>To make all this possible,</b>

122
00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:43.125
<b>she sacrifices so much.</b>

123
00:08:43.125 --> 00:08:49.458
<b>Understanding this sacrifice in your heart is </b>
<b>the first step of true gratitude.</b>

124
00:08:49.458 --> 00:08:56.625
<b>Then, children and family must express this </b>
<b>gratitude not just through words,</b>

125
00:08:56.625 --> 00:09:00.458
<b>but through their actions.</b>

126
00:09:00.458 --> 00:09:07.291
<b>They must strive to make that mother's life easier,</b>

127
00:09:07.291 --> 00:09:10.458
<b>understanding what support she needs.</b>

128
00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:19.083
<b>In essence, this simply means that </b>
<b>gratitude is essential within the family.</b>

129
00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:22.583
<b>And this feeling must be expressed </b>
<b>not only through words</b>

130
00:09:22.583 --> 00:09:23.666
<b>but</b>

131
00:09:23.666 --> 00:09:33.500
<b>through our conduct and</b>
<b>actions towards each other.</b>

132
00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.166
<b>Reflect on this!</b>

133
00:09:39.541 --> 00:09:41.791
<b>Any business organization</b>

134
00:09:41.791 --> 00:09:46.458
<b>can only succeed through the interconnected </b>
<b>relationships of many people -</b>

135
00:09:46.458 --> 00:09:48.166
<b>be they employees,</b>

136
00:09:48.166 --> 00:09:49.291
<b>customers,</b>

137
00:09:49.291 --> 00:09:52.166
<b>or other partners.</b>

138
00:09:52.166 --> 00:10:01.416
<b>In such a setting, it becomes crucial for </b>
<b>any leader to keep all these stakeholders happy.</b>

139
00:10:01.416 --> 00:10:04.583
<b>But how can this be achieved?</b>

140
00:10:04.583 --> 00:10:07.958
<b>The first essential step is this:</b>

141
00:10:07.958 --> 00:10:11.666
<b>In your business journey, </b>
<b>every diligent employee,</b>

142
00:10:11.666 --> 00:10:14.583
<b>every loyal partner, and every valued customer</b>

143
00:10:14.583 --> 00:10:21.291
<b>nurture sincere gratitude in your heart for their contribution.</b>

144
00:10:21.291 --> 00:10:23.958
<b>To achieve this, one must understand</b>

145
00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:29.541
<b>that each person, whether their </b>
<b>role seems small or large,</b>

146
00:10:29.541 --> 00:10:33.333
<b>makes a vital contribution to your business.</b>

147
00:10:33.333 --> 00:10:40.500
<b>But is merely feeling grateful </b>
<b>in your heart enough?</b>

148
00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.625
<b>Having gratitude in your mind</b>

149
00:10:43.625 --> 00:10:46.416
<b>but not expressing it</b>

150
00:10:46.416 --> 00:10:57.416
<b>is like buying a beautiful gift, </b>
<b>wrapping it elegantly,</b>

151
00:10:57.416 --> 00:11:05.208
<b>but forgetting to give it to </b>
<b>the person it was meant for.</b>

152
00:11:05.208 --> 00:11:07.208
<b>Don't make this mistake.</b>

153
00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:10.083
<b>Express the gratitude in your heart.</b>

154
00:11:10.083 --> 00:11:12.875
<b>Begin with verbal appreciation.</b>

155
00:11:12.875 --> 00:11:17.375
<b>A heartfelt 'thank you' carries immense power.</b>

156
00:11:17.375 --> 00:11:20.166
<b>But don't stop there.</b>

157
00:11:20.166 --> 00:11:23.625
<b>Don't hold back in showing appreciation.</b>

158
00:11:23.625 --> 00:11:30.666
<b>Share the fruits of success with those whose </b>
<b>partnership helped achieve it.</b>

159
00:11:30.666 --> 00:11:35.750
<b>Whether it's gratitude in your heart </b>
<b>or profits in your business,</b>

160
00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.041
<b>make sure to share them with others.</b>

161
00:11:38.041 --> 00:11:44.375
<b>One who shares from the</b>
<b>heart never finds their reserves empty.</b>

162
00:11:44.375 --> 00:11:46.166
<b>Reflect on this!</b>

